34
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,040
Oh, wow. Right. You lose the funding too.

35
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:45,130
Exactly. Delivering that primary policy promise early

36
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:51,400
in wave two proves the system actually works, and it maintains momentum for the heavy lifting later.

37
00:02:51,440 --> 00:03:01,020
That makes perfect sense. So you secure the early win, programs stop keeping isolated lists, and then in wave three, you can finally justify the heavy investment for that data exchange

